{
  "case_id": "2018-18-281",
  "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Virginia House of Delegates",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2011, the Virginia House of Delegates formulated a redistricting plan that garnered overwhelming bipartisan support and swift preclearance by the Justice Department. That plan has governed the first four election cycles of the decade and delivered on its promise to provide African American voters with the ability to elect their candidates of choice in 12 districts that everybody agreed should be majority-minority districts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Mr. Clement, there are two -- as I understand it, you're -- you're claiming standing on two theories. One is -- and correct me if I'm wrong. One is that you're representing the Commonwealth. The other is that you're representing the House as an institution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, in those off-year elections, the single-most important data point would be a contested primary, because, especially in districts that are going to be relatively democratic where you really figure out whether or not the African American voters get to vote for their candidate of choice is in a contested primary, because that's when you have an African American candidate of choice going head-to-head with a white Democrat."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Well, Justice Kagan, I don't think it was quite that cursory. And there was -- there was some other information from other districts, but I think the critical thing is there was a consideration that all these districts share similar problems in not"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Well, it is odd, Mr. Clement, that you say they didn't have voting records because 95 is next to 92. And what the district court did there was to look at both individually and then their impact on each."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. RATNER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I have two points on standing and two on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- suppose that you're right that the legislature has no interest in who is going to represent each district. But I understood Mr. Clement to be making another argument, which is the legislature does have an interest in represent -- representational processes working correctly and that what something like this does is it confuses the representational process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. RATNER: So let me give you two responses, Justice Kagan. The -- the first is that I don't think it's true that there are current blurred lines of accountability. In fact, under the Virginia constitution, Article II, Section 6, it's clear that legislators represent their current district."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Virginia State Board of Elections",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HEYTENS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: There is only one sovereign whose law was declared unconstitutional by the federal district court. And what this Court is essentially being asked to do is to referee a dispute within the Virginia state government about whether Virginia should appeal that decision to this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So tell me who you think -- who you think can challenge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just a couple quick points on standing and on the merits. First on standing, I don't think you can underestimate the impact of this case and the decision below and the remedial order that follows on the House and the way it operates day to day. The remedial order reconfigured 25 of the 100 seats. That's fully 25 percent of the House's seats. That's much more than a peppercorn. I don't think the solution is to get 25 individual members here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Clement, what do we do now? If we rule in your favor and say that every House that has -- creates a plan has standing, we invite complete discord in a state over who represents the interests of that law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The difference between the districts here and the districts in Alabama are completely stark. You looked at a district in Alabama, and they moved out 16,000 people and only 30 -- or in 16,000 people, only 36 of whom were white. Here, with HD 69, there's a 1 percent difference in the racial makeup of the people who went in and out of the district, 44 versus 43 percent. The -- you cannot say that race predominated here, faithfully with this Court's precedence about what predominance means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-281",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10a1d56b72d2b87ea1cc70d5647b04824194789311dbc840d8c6ac90b80949ee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10a1d56b72d2-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
